<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 21.72 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 21.72 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month discount Treasury bills fell to 21.72 at an auction on Tuesday from 22.15 at the last auction on April 15, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   Apr 22	     Apr 15</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K2407973     KZ43K1707977</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  500		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 2,000		1,200</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 784.4		500.0</p>
<p> Average price			 94.85 pct	  94.76</p>
<p> Average yield			 21.72		22.12</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				July 24, 1997    July 17, 1997</p>
<p>The finance ministry is also auctioning 650 million tenge of six-month GKOs on April 28 and 600 million tenge of three-month bills on April 29. The government will also repay 580 million tenge in maturing three-month paper on April 24.</p>
<p>NOTE - The finance ministry has renamed treasury bills MKMs, using the Kazakh abbreviation, instead of the Russian GKO.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
